  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improvement of livelihoods through sustainable agriculture</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project began in 2006, focusing on two very vulnerable districts: Khulna, a saline-affected area in south west Bangladesh; and Rajshahi, a drought-prone district in the north west.  Caritas works primarily with marginalised landless farmers (&#x201c;landless&#x201d; being a technical term which includes those who own small amounts of land, insufficient of themselves to support a family).  Training is provided in farming methods which can increase production and which are also environmentally sustainable.  For example, communities are introduced to drought-resistant plant varieties, composting and water conservation techniques, crop diversification and integrated crop management, and ways to enhance soil fertility.  Families are also helped to make the most of the food available through better knowledge of nutrition and the importance of eating vegetables.  The project also seeks to raise rural incomes.  Communities are helped to address the problems arising from climate change, and to be prepared and have contingency plans in place in the event of natural disaster (drought, flooding etc).</narrative>
  </description>
